<title>HONG KONG: Barclays HK branch places US$20 mln FRCD.</title>
<headline>Barclays HK branch places US$20 mln FRCD.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Barclays Bank Plc's Hong Kong branch has lodged a US$20 million floating rate certificates of deposit issue due May 16, 2002, with the Hong Kong Monetary Authority Central Moneymarkets Units.</p>
<p>The five-year certificates were issued at par to float at 10 basis points over the three-month London Interbank Offered Rate.</p>
<p>The minimum denomination is US$250,000.</p>
<p>Schroders Asia was the arranger and paying agent.</p>
<p>The payment date is May 16.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6960</p>
</text>
